// PhishAlert — psl.js
// Registrable-domain ("eTLD+1") lookup based on the Mozilla Public Suffix List
// (https://publicsuffix.org, MPL-2.0; snapshot fetched 2026-10-04, ICANN + private sections).
//
// Why this exists: taking the last two labels of a hostname treats "sbi.co.in" and
// "evil.co.in" as the same domain ("co.in"), which silently disabled Reply-To,
// link-text and thread-hijack checks for .co.in, .gov.in, .co.uk, .com.au and
// every other multi-part suffix. Private-section entries (github.io, pages.dev,
// blogspot.com, ...) are included on purpose: two tenants of a shared host are
// different owners, and these hosts are routinely abused for phishing pages.
//
// Loaded as a content script (before content-shared.js) and via importScripts()
// in the background service worker, so both sides use identical logic.
// Regenerate with: python3 gen.py  (reads publicsuffix/list public_suffix_list.dat).
